```

Note: `householdId` and `customerCode` have plain getters/setters; `address`/`city`/`telephone` carry `@NotEmpty` (telephone also `@Pattern` E.164).

## 2. Owner creation endpoint (POST) — YAML + function classes

There is exactly ONE POST YAML under `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/` for creating owners:

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`

It defines the full pipeline (each `next:` chains to the following step):

```
validate  -> ValidateOwnerFields
unique    -> CheckUniqueTelephone     (govern: transaction)
household -> CheckUniqueHousehold     (govern: transaction)
build     -> BuildOwner               (govern: transaction)
household-assign -> AssignHousehold   (govern: transaction)
customerCode     -> AssignCustomerCode(govern: transaction)
save      -> SaveOwner                (govern: transaction)
respond   -> RespondWithOwnerCreated  (govern: transaction)
```
Top of file: `authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"`.

The "second" owner-creation-related YAML you may be thinking of is not under `rest/` but under `src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/` — these wire the exception handlers:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.MissingOwnerFieldsException.yml`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateHouseholdException.yml` (contents: `handle: class: ...DuplicateHouseholdExceptionHandler`)

Function classes (all in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`):
- `ValidateOwnerFields.java`, `CheckUniqueTelephone.java`, `CheckUniqueHousehold.java`, `BuildOwner.java`, `AssignHousehold.java`, `AssignCustomerCode.java`, `SaveOwner.java`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`

## 3. Required-field check for address (validation)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerFields.java`

```java
public void service(@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, Out<OwnerFieldsDto> validated)
        throws MissingOwnerFieldsException, InvalidTelephoneException, InvalidEmailException {
    List<String> missing = new ArrayList<>();
    require(missing, "firstName", request.getFirstName());
    require(missing, "lastName", request.getLastName());
    require(missing, "address", request.getAddress());   // <-- address required-field check
    require(missing, "city", request.getCity());
    require(missing, "telephone", request.getTelephone());
    if (!missing.isEmpty()) throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(missing);
    request.setTelephone(OwnerTelephone.toE164(request.getTelephone()));
    OwnerEmail.normalize(request);
    validated.set(request);                              // republishes as @Val for later steps
}
private static void require(List<String> missing, String field, String value) {
    if (value == null || value.isBlank()) missing.add(field);
}
```

`MissingOwnerFieldsException` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/MissingOwnerFieldsException.java`) carries the field list; handled with HTTP 400 by `MissingOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler.java` in the same package. (There is currently NO address-normalization step — the acceptance tests in section 5 expect one but no such code exists yet.)

## 4. Household duplicate detection + shared household id

Duplicate detection: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CheckUniqueHousehold.java`

```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
        throws DuplicateHouseholdException {
    if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) return;      // opt-out
    String lastName = normalize(request.getLastName());
    String address = normalize(request.getAddress());
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (lastName.equals(normalize(existing.getLastName()))
